;docs/ai_digest/mesh_net.md: how the services find each other and settle which of a pair makes the link
(defq s (dia-scene) blue 0xffd7e6f7 green 0xffdff0d8 gold 0xffffe8a8 grey 0xfff2f4f6 dark 0xff202428)
(dia-put s 'a (dia-box '("machine A" "system id 3F..") 150 48 gold 11 :first) 0 40)
(dia-put s 'b (dia-box '("machine B" "system id 9C..") 150 48 blue 11 :first) 380 40)
(dia-put s 'c (dia-box '("machine C" "on another network" "hears no beacon") 150 62 blue 11 :first) 380 190)
(dia-join s 'a 'b "each hears the other's beacon" :both)
(dia-join s 'b 'c "a link made by name, mesh -t" :both)
(dia-put s 'hello (dia-box '("a hello, every 2 seconds" "who I have heard from, myself," "and where each listens") 200 62 green 11 :first) 0 183)
(dia-join s 'hello 'c "B tells C of A")
(dia-say s "1  A and B both know where the other is, so the lower system id dials, A. B waits, 15 seconds, then dials itself." 0 282 11)
(dia-say s "2  Only one of a pair knows where the other is: it dials." 0 298 11)
(dia-say s "3  Every service tells every other who it has heard, a hello. So C, that hears no beacon, learns of A from B, and links to it." 0 314 11)
(dia-say s "4  A dial that brings no link is tried again after twice as long, 10 seconds, 20, 40, 80." 0 330 11)
(dia-say s "5  A peer not heard of for 30 seconds, by its beacon or in anyone's hello, is forgotten." 0 346 11)
(dia-say s "So each machine has one link to each other, and none is on the way between two." 0 20 12 :nil dark)
(diagram "mesh_dial" (dia-scene-doc s))
